## Edge cases

- Historical OOS records may lack `Filed URL`. Join by `Filed OOS issue #N` / `Filed as #N` when present; otherwise skip and count in a skipped bucket.
- Historical source issues may have no comments in the fetched dump. Treat combined-away as unknown unless another marker is present.
- A closed issue can have no PR link and no not-planned signal. Keep it provisional and report `closed_unknown`.
- Multiple log records can point at the same filed issue. Score each distinct canonical stable id separately; dedupe only exact duplicate evidence keys.
- A single filed issue may aggregate several OOS items. Count each canonical stable id once per reviewer token derived from its accepted block.
- Security-held OOS without a public issue URL must not be scored as filed OOS.
- Legacy code-review OOS blocks use `FINDING_N` ids; ndjson stable ids and legacy body citations must match via `_issue_covers_stable_id` rules, not bare suffix equality alone.
- `oos-accepted-main-agent` items use `Main agent` when ndjson stable id matches main-agent source rules and no round markdown block exists.
- Cap-rollup ndjson may list only one stable id while round markdown retains many member blocks; expansion must score every unattached member block against the rollup URL.
- Same-run `OOS_1` in multiple artifacts must never share reviewer attribution through bare-suffix-only indexing.

## Failure modes

- If `gh issue list --json comments,stateReason` is unsupported, `fetch_main` may fail. If that happens during implementation, use the smallest compatible fallback:
  - Retry without optional fields.
  - Render the fate section with degraded combined-away and state-reason detection.
  - Print a short warning in the section.
- If `larch-logs` is missing, render `No filed OOS run-log evidence found.` and continue.
- If an issue URL points outside the fetched repo, skip it and count it as skipped.
- If implement ndjson exists without any accepted markdown in the same run, attribute reviewer as `unknown` but still score by stable id or URL when possible; cap-rollup expansion may still recover multiple rows from rollup prose alone.

